= Chiang Kai-shek appointed Commander-in-Chief

After gaining control over the Guomindang and solidifying control over Guangdong, Chiang Kai-shek has been appointed the Commander-in-Chief of the National Revolutionary Army.

Along with this, he is now the commander of the Northern Expedition. Because of this, foreigners have begun calling him the "Red General"

Now, Chiang Kai-shek has obtained the highest military rank possible to command several generals and distinguish his control:

*Generalissimo.*
